==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|corium|lang=la||leather}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|coria}}

# {{anatomy}} The inner layer of [[skin]], the [[dermis]].
# {{anatomy}} The deep layer of [[mucous membrane]]s beneath the [[epithelium]].
# {{historical}} [[armour|Armour]] made of [[leather]], particularly that used by the [[Roman]]s.
#: {{rfquotek|Fosbroke}}

===Etymology 2===
{{suffix|core|ium}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{nuclear physics}} The [[lavalike]] material produced in a nuclear [[meltdown]].
#* {{cite-book|year=1991|title=Numerical modelling of basic heat transfer phenomena in nuclear systems|author=Franklin Chung and L.E. Hochreiter|page=32|passage=Previous studies of the thermal behavior of '''corium''' in a degraded nuclear reactor have focussed primarily on the process of heat transfer within the '''corium'''.}}
